  "data_abstract": "New measurements are presented for charged hadron azimuthal correlations at mid-rapidity in Au+Au collissions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 62.4 and 200 GeV. They are compared to earlier measurements obtained at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 130 GeV and in Pb+Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 17.2 GeV. Sizeable anisotropies are observed with centrality and transverse momentum ($p_T$) dependence characteristic of elliptic flow ($v_2$). For a broad range of centralities, the observed magnitudes and trends of the differential anisotropy, $v_2$($p_T$), change very little over the collision energy range $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 62-200 GeV, indicating saturation of the excitation function for $v_2$ at these energies. Sucha a saturation may be indicative of the dominance of a very soft equation of state for $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ ~ 60-200 GeV.\n",
